Original commit body from d04b84b34676242e08b60b0edd7063cc4b0b131e:

The cross-language demoter mapped .json/.yaml/.yml/.toml/.xml/.html to a
pseudo-language "config" and hard-excluded any candidate whose short name
appeared as a substring in three such files. Its own rationale is
cross-language DISPATCH -- an HTTP route, an RPC method, an FFI name --
and a YAML file mentioning a Python symbol is a manifest, not a
dispatcher.

MEASURED BEFORE CODING: 112 of 207 demotions (54%) had fewer than three
hits in any real other-language file. The worst shapes make the case
better than the ratio: extract (66 config hits, 1 code), matches (30, 1),
_label (24, ZERO) -- a leading-underscore private helper with no
cross-language dispatch story at all, deleted from the report by
substring collisions in YAML.

TWO HALVES, ONE CHANGE, because either alone is wrong.
(A) The threshold now reads only real other-language files. This is what
    the invariant's statement compels -- "a substring collision between
    its short name and a non-code manifest file is not such evidence" --
    not a judgement made here. The manifest tally is KEPT and published
    per candidate as config_name_hits; the signal is demoted, not deleted.
(D) The demotions that remain are DISCLOSED in a cross_language_demoted
    listing, the treatment entrypoint_only_dead and
    test_only_reachable_candidates already get. It is always present and
    empty when nothing was demoted, so a reader can tell "the demoter ran
    and took nothing" from "this view does not say". The text renderer
    gains the same line unconditionally.

(A) alone is a one-directional loosening; (D) alone leaves the statement
violated.

MEASURED EFFECT on this repository: dead candidates 2282 -> 2402 (+120),
demotions 207 -> 87, all 87 now listed. The 34 non-test python __init__
methods no default run could show come back -- the cohort whose
invisibility manufactured INV-rolok's "0 of 2,152 dead candidates are
__init__" sizing claim.

DEAD_CODE_MAYBE_SCHEMA_VERSION 0.2.0 -> 0.3.0, additive: nothing removed
or renamed, so a 0.2.0 reader keeps working.

Addresses INV-hugit -- closed after merge, with the merge SHA as
evidence.

